# Project Lifecycle (Publishing OS)

## Overview

This document defines the end-to-end lifecycle of a book project within Publishing OS, from initial idea through to publication and marketing.

Every AI agent in the system operates at a specific stage of this lifecycle. The lifecycle ensures consistency, repeatability, and clear responsibility boundaries between agents.

---

# Stage 1: Idea Capture

## Input

* Topic or niche idea

## Process

A book idea is submitted manually or generated via future market discovery tools.

## Output

* Raw project request

---

# Stage 2: Project Initialization

## Agent: Project Manager

## Process

* Creates a unique Project ID
* Generates folder structure
* Initializes project.json
* Sets default parameters:

  * Target audience
  * Estimated word count
  * Project status = "initiated"

## Output

* Structured project file
* Project workspace created

---

# Stage 3: Market Validation

## Agent: Market Research

## Process

* Analyzes niche demand
* Identifies reader pain points
* Reviews competition
* Evaluates profitability potential
* Suggests positioning angle

## Output

* Market analysis report
* Recommendation: proceed / revise / reject

---

# Stage 4: Book Planning

## Agent: Book Planner

## Process

* Defines book promise
* Identifies target reader avatar
* Creates chapter outline
* Defines learning progression
* Assigns estimated word counts per chapter

## Output

* Full book outline
* Book structure document

---

# Stage 5: Research

## Agent: Research Agent

## Process

* Gathers structured information per chapter:

  * Best practices
  * Technical knowledge
  * Safety considerations
  * Tools and materials
  * Common mistakes
  * Step-by-step processes

## Output

* Chapter research packets

---

# Stage 6: Chapter Briefing

## Agent: Chapter Brief Agent

## Process

* Converts research into structured writing instructions
* Defines:

  * Objective
  * Key points
  * Required sections
  * Warnings
  * Examples

## Output

* Chapter brief documents

---

# Stage 7: Writing

## Agent: Writing Agent

## Process

* Converts chapter briefs into full chapters
* Maintains consistent tone and style
* Includes practical examples and checklists
* Avoids introducing new unsupported facts

## Output

* Draft chapters

---

# Stage 8: Editing

## Agent: Editing Agent

## Process

* Improves clarity and flow
* Removes repetition
* Ensures consistent tone
* Fixes grammar and structure issues

## Output

* Edited chapters

---

# Stage 9: Quality Assurance

## Agent: QA Agent

## Process

* Checks for:

  * Missing sections
  * Logical inconsistencies
  * Hallucinated or unsupported claims
  * Safety concerns
  * Structural issues

## Output

* Approval or revision request

---

# Stage 10: Book Assembly

## Agent: Book Assembly Agent

## Process

* Combines all chapters into final manuscript
* Adds:

  * Introduction
  * Conclusion
  * Table of contents
  * Glossary
  * Resources section

## Output

* Complete manuscript

---

# Stage 11: Publishing Metadata

## Agent: Metadata Agent

## Process

* Generates:

  * Title options
  * Subtitle
  * Description
  * Keywords
  * Categories
  * Author bio

## Output

* Publishing-ready metadata package

---

# Stage 12: Formatting (Future Phase)

## Agent: Formatter (Phase 2)

## Process

* Converts manuscript into:

  * EPUB
  * PDF
  * Print-ready file

## Output

* Formatted book files

---

# Stage 13: Publication (Future Phase)

## Agent: Publishing Agent (Phase 2)

## Process

* Uploads to platforms (e.g. Amazon KDP)
* Applies metadata
* Confirms publication status

## Output

* Published book listing

---

# Stage 14: Marketing (Future Phase)

## Agent: Marketing Agent (Phase 2)

## Process

* Generates promotional content:

  * Social media posts
  * Blog articles
  * Email sequences
  * Short-form video scripts

## Output

* Marketing asset package

---

# Lifecycle Principles

## Linear Flow (Default)

The system is designed as a linear pipeline from idea → publication.

Each stage depends on the output of the previous stage.

---

## Feedback Loops

Certain stages may loop:

* QA → Writing (if issues found)
* Editing → Writing (if clarity issues persist)
* Market Research → Book Planning (if positioning is weak)

---

## Human Oversight

Human review is recommended at:

* Market validation stage
* Final QA stage
* Publishing stage

---

## Modularity

Each stage is handled by a dedicated agent.

Agents can be improved or replaced without changing the entire system.

---

# Future Extensions

The lifecycle is designed to expand into:

* Multi-book batch generation
* Automated niche discovery
* Continuous content publishing
* Multi-platform distribution
* AI-assisted marketing ecosystems
